  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Sunosi (solriamfetol), a DNRI / wakefulness-promoting agent; effective 2019-11-20. Approval gates and the explicit MAOI contraindication encoded. Source denial list mirrors approval failures; no duplicate denials. Documentation and therapy attestations require manual review.",
    "Underlying airway obstruction requires CPAP or a similar device for at least 90 days and throughout Sunosi treatment. OSA gates are indication-specific; the narcolepsy path also checks for coexisting obstruction. Sunosi is not indicated for treatment of underlying airway obstruction.",
    "Cautions: MAOI use within 14 days is contraindicated (encoded). Monitor heart rate and blood pressure prior to and throughout therapy; avoid use in patients with serious heart problems. For history of psychosis or bipolar disorder, doses may need reduction or discontinuation if psychiatric symptoms arise. Schedule IV controlled substance with potential for abuse.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 30 × 75mg tablets/month and 30 × 150mg tablets/month. No numeric quantity enforcement; manual review required."
  ],
